       mmyyttooooll reads each _i_n_p_u_t, or the standard input when none is named, and writes the result to the standard output.

       A second paragraph explains the model the reader needs: what goes in, what comes out, and what is never changed.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       --vv     Report each _i_n_p_u_t on the standard error as it is read.

       --oo _f_i_l_e
              Write to _f_i_l_e instead of the standard output.

       --hh     Print a short usage summary.

       ----hheellpp Show this manual.

